# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pepcal environment
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. All variables are optional at first run.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

# When these two are BOTH set, the app uses Supabase Auth (Google SSO)
# and the real Postgres backend with row-level security — see supabase/migrations.
# When either is missing/blank, the app runs in DEMO MODE: a local-only,
# on-this-browser store seeded with clearly-labelled fictional data and no
# account. This makes the app fully runnable before any cloud setup.
# Only the project URL and anon key belong in NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables.
# Never put a Supabase service-role key or Google client secret here.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web Push (notifications) — wired in the next build phase.
# Generate with: npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# The public key is safe to ship to the browser; the private key is a
# server secret and must never be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:you@example.com
